        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">You can walk barefoot on a treadmill, but most people should
            not.</strong> Many manuals tell you to wear athletic shoes, and bare feet are exposed to
            friction burns, scrapes, blisters and toes caught at the hood or side rails. Socks are
            slipperier still.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Wear a well-fitting walking or running shoe with a grippy rubber sole, keep the safety key
            clipped on, and if you have diabetes or reduced feeling in your feet, ask your doctor
            about footwear before you start. For the rest of the basics, see our
